                <div class="container pdp-recipe-description-banner-wrapper js-swiper-refresh pb-3">

                </div>
                <div class="pdp-desc border-top-grey border-lg-0">

                    <div class="d-flex flex-column flex-lg-column-reverse">

    <div class="collapsible-md pb-lg-5 mt-3 mb-3 mb-lg-5 border-bottom-grey">
        <h2 class="title mb-3 d-lg-none libre-caslon font-weight-normal">
            Ingredients
        </h2>
        <div class="value content">
            <div class="recipe-ingredients d-flex flex-row-reverse row js-copy-to-clipboard-target ">

                    <div class="col-12  recipe-ingredients-second-col mb-3 mb-lg-0">
                        <h2 class="libre-caslon d-none d-lg-block font-weight-normal mb-3 mb-lg-4">
                            Ingredients
                        </h2>
                        <ul class="ingredients-list">

                                <li class="line common-desc-text libre-caslon name" itemprop="recipeIngredient">
                                    9 ounces Perdue Grilled Chicken Breast Strips
                                </li>

                                <li class="line common-desc-text libre-caslon name" itemprop="recipeIngredient">
                                    1/2 cup Parmesan cheese
                                </li>

                                <li class="line common-desc-text libre-caslon name" itemprop="recipeIngredient">
                                    2 cups shredded mozzarella cheese
                                </li>

                                <li class="line common-desc-text libre-caslon name" itemprop="recipeIngredient">
                                    10 ounces garlic and herb cheese
                                </li>

                                <li class="line common-desc-text libre-caslon name" itemprop="recipeIngredient">
                                    1 cup artichoke hearts, finely chopped
                                </li>

                                <li class="line common-desc-text libre-caslon name" itemprop="recipeIngredient">
                                    1 (16-ounce) can refrigerated pizza dough
                                </li>

                        </ul>
                    </div>

            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

                    </div>
                    <div class="recipe-steps pdp-desc">

        <div class="collapsible-md recipe-step pb-lg-5 my-3 mb-lg-5 border-bottom-grey">
            <h2 class="title mb-3 d-lg-none libre-caslon font-weight-normal" >
                Step 1
            </h2>
            <div class="value content">
                <div class="d-flex flex-column d-lg-block">

                        <img class="img-fluid float-lg-left mr-lg-5" src="/images/products/100012_chickencheesebread_step1.jpg" alt="Recipe step image" />

                    <div class="clearfix">
                        <h2 class="d-none d-lg-block libre-caslon font-weight-normal mb-0 pb-lg-4 pt-lg-2">
                            Step 1
                        </h2>
                        <div class="recipe-step-desc common-desc-text pb-4 pb-lg-0 pt-lg-0 libre-caslon" itemprop="recipeInstructions">
                            Preheat oven to 350 F. Using a food processor or two forks (one in each hand), shred chicken strips. In a bowl, combine the shredded chicken, shredded mozzarella, garlic-herb cheese, chopped artichokes and Parmesan cheese. Mix well.
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="collapsible-md recipe-step pb-lg-5 my-3 mb-lg-5 border-bottom-grey">
            <h2 class="title mb-3 d-lg-none libre-caslon font-weight-normal">
                Step 2
            </h2>
            <div class="value content">
                <div class="d-flex flex-column d-lg-block">

                        <img class="img-fluid float-lg-right ml-lg-5" src="/images/products/100012_chickencheesebread_step2.jpg" alt="Recipe step image" />

                    <div class="clearfix">
                        <h2 class="mb-0 pb-lg-4 d-none d-lg-block libre-caslon font-weight-normal pt-lg-2">
                            Step 2
                        </h2>
                        <div class="recipe-step-desc common-desc-text pb-4 pb-lg-0 pt-lg-0 libre-caslon" itemprop="recipeInstructions">
                            On a lightly floured surface, roll out the pizza dough into a 12 x 18-inch rectangle. With a pizza cutter or a sharp knife, cut the dough into 16 (3 x 4-inch) rectangles. Dollop a heaping tablespoon of chicken mixture onto each dough rectangle. Leave one rectangle without the spread and set aside. Press the mixture to evenly cover each rectangle.
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="collapsible-md recipe-step pb-lg-5 my-3 mb-lg-5 border-bottom-grey">
            <h2 class="title mb-3 d-lg-none libre-caslon font-weight-normal">
                Step 3
            </h2>
            <div class="value content">
                <div class="d-flex flex-column d-lg-block">

                        <img class="img-fluid float-lg-left mr-lg-5" src="/images/products/100012_chickencheesebread_step3.jpg" alt="Recipe step image" />

                    <div class="clearfix">
                        <h2 class="mb-0 pb-lg-4 d-none d-lg-block libre-caslon font-weight-normal pt-lg-2">
                            Step 3
                        </h2>
                        <div class="recipe-step-desc common-desc-text pb-4 pb-lg-0 pt-lg-0 libre-caslon" itemprop="recipeInstructions">
                            Spray a 9 x 5-inch loaf pan with cooking spray and prop it up vertically. Use a spatula to layer the rectangles into stacks of 3 or 4. Place the stacked layers into the loaf pan, chicken side up. Top with the uncoated dough rectangle that you set aside. Sit the pan horizontally.
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="collapsible-md recipe-step pb-lg-5 my-3 mb-lg-5 border-bottom-grey">
            <h2 class="title mb-3 d-lg-none libre-caslon font-weight-normal">
                Step 4
            </h2>
            <div class="value content">
                <div class="d-flex flex-column d-lg-block">

                        <img class="img-fluid float-lg-right ml-lg-5" src="/images/products/100012_chickencheesebread_step4.jpg" alt="Recipe step image" />

                    <div class="clearfix">
                        <h2 class="mb-0 pb-lg-4 d-none d-lg-block libre-caslon font-weight-normal pt-lg-2">
                            Step 4
                        </h2>
                        <div class="recipe-step-desc common-desc-text pb-4 pb-lg-0 pt-lg-0 libre-caslon" itemprop="recipeInstructions">
                            Bake the loaf for 1 hour, or until well browned and cooked through. Let cool for 5 minutes and then turn the loaf out of the pan. Serve while warm and let people peel off their slices.
<br><br>
TIP: The inside stays just a bit doughy due to the moisture in the chicken, so make sure to cook it until the top begins to brown.
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

